/// Contracts: wire types generated by wehoop-api `pnpm gen:swift` (GameChange, the
/// LiveEvent bodies, Pulse, Snapshot, the `/changes` page, `/v1/players/:id`, the
/// `league:{code}:scores` message and the `v_schedule` / `v_boxscore` / `v_standings` /
/// `v_player_seasons` rows). Codable, Hashable and `Sendable`, no dependencies.
///
/// `Generated/` is never edited by hand: `scripts/sync-contracts.sh` regenerates it from
/// a wehoop-api checkout and records the backend commit in `scripts/contracts-source`;
/// CI checks out that commit and fails when the files differ from what its schemas emit.
///
/// Open unions (backend plan rev 4.11 (5)): every code enum has `case unknown(String)`,
/// and `GameChange` / `LiveEvent` decode a `type` this build does not know as
/// `.unknown(raw)` with their shared fields (envelope, period, score) intact, so a new
/// league, period type, status or change type never breaks decoding or sequencing.
/// Ids and timestamps are `String` here; WehoopData maps them to Domain types once.

/// Where the generated contract files come from.
public enum ContractsSource {
    /// The backend command that emits this module's files.
    public static let generator = "pnpm gen:swift"
}
